<title>USA: TABLE-Gargoyles Inc Q2 profit rises.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Gargoyles Inc Q2 profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>KENT, Wash. 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Qtr Mos ended 6/30  6 Mos ended 6/30</p>
<p>			  1997	 1996	  1997	   1996</p>
<p> Net sales   $16,334,074 $10,632,523 $24,532,340 $17,626,816</p>
<p> Cost of sales 6,008,470   4,520,790   9,090,467   7,386,185</p>
<p> Gross profit 10,325,604   6,111,733  15,441,873  10,240,631</p>
<p> License income  221,736     132,663     331,736     293,609</p>
<p>Operating expenses:</p>
<p>   Sales &amp; mktg 5,396,833   2,617,767   8,186,038   4,985,350</p>
<p>   Genl &amp; admin 1,600,820   1,108,618   2,757,821   2,077,552</p>
<p>Shipping and</p>
<p>   warehousing  1,045,387     792,181   1,454,417   1,070,638</p>
<p>   R&amp;D		398,865     197,602     764,156     332,658</p>
<p>   Stock compensation --    3,503,640	    --   3,528,140</p>
<p>Total oper expnss 8,441,905 8,219,808 13,162,432  11,994,338  Income-ops     2,105,435  (1,975,412)  2,611,177  (1,460,098)</p>
<p>Total other income (500,060) (629,599) (473,269)  (1,160,837)  Net income     1,284,375 (2,605,011)   1,709,908 (2,620,935)</p>
<p> Net EPS		 0.17	(0.46)	  0.22	(0.46)</p>
<p> Shrs outstanding 7,689,283 5,712,078   7,686,083   5,710,896</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 results include a $3.5 million nonrecurring stock compensation charge.  Adjusted for this charge, Q2 1996 pro forma net income was $720,000, or $0.13 per share.</p>
<p>Gross margin increased to 63.2% for the quarter ended June 30, 1997 from 57.5% for the quarter ended June 30, 1996.</p>
